WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.201
-Our next guest
is a talented actress

00:00:02.201 --> 00:00:03.703
you know best from
"The Bold Type,"

00:00:03.703 --> 00:00:06.138
"One Life to Live,"
and Broadway's "Next to Normal."

00:00:06.138 --> 00:00:08.908
She's starring in the second
season of "The White Lotus,"

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:11.177
which airs Sunday nights
on HBO and HBO Max.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:12.245
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.279
-He's so handsome.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:17.250
He has blond hair
and these big blue eyes.

00:00:17.250 --> 00:00:19.118
[ Chuckles ]

00:00:19.118 --> 00:00:21.621
[ Chuckling ]
He's really funny, too.

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:25.225
I spend more time with him
than Cameron sometimes

00:00:25.225 --> 00:00:27.127
'cause he's so busy at work.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:31.030
Such a cutie.

00:00:31.030 --> 00:00:32.231
Want to see a pic?

00:00:32.231 --> 00:00:40.773 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:40.773 --> 00:00:49.348 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:49.348 --> 00:00:52.552
-This is just a picture
of your kids.

00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:54.053
-Is it?

00:00:54.053 --> 00:00:55.521
Whoopsie.

00:00:55.521 --> 00:00:58.891
-Please welcome to the show
Meghann Fahy, everybody.

00:00:58.891 --> 00:01:00.993
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:00.993 --> 00:01:07.099 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:07.099 --> 00:01:13.239 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:13.239 --> 00:01:15.708
How are you?
-Oh, I'm great.

00:01:15.708 --> 00:01:18.077
I'm so happy to be here.
-I'm so happy to have you.

00:01:18.077 --> 00:01:21.046
I'm also very happy this is
your first time on the show.

00:01:21.046 --> 00:01:23.416
But we also -- It's the first
time we've had your family

00:01:23.416 --> 00:01:25.818
in the audience,
which is very exciting for us.

00:01:25.818 --> 00:01:27.921
-I don't know where they are.

00:01:27.921 --> 00:01:29.855
Oh, there they are.
Hi, guys.

00:01:29.855 --> 00:01:32.425
-I'm so glad. I was worried
they'd be way farther back.

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:35.928
Be like, "Why did we give them
such bad seats?"

00:01:35.928 --> 00:01:37.463
This is great to have you here.

00:01:37.463 --> 00:01:38.497
This is the first time
on our show.

00:01:38.497 --> 00:01:40.900
But you have been
in this building before,

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:43.369
because there's a very important
person in your life

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:44.437
who is located here.

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.239
-That's right.
My dentist.

00:01:46.239 --> 00:01:47.706
-Your dentist.
-Yeah, yeah.

00:01:47.706 --> 00:01:50.276
-A lot of people don't know
that, but 30 Rock has a lot

00:01:50.276 --> 00:01:52.778
of non-show-business people
operating out of here.

00:01:52.778 --> 00:01:55.548
-Yeah, and very important
non-business-show people, too.

00:01:55.548 --> 00:01:57.082
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:01:57.082 --> 00:01:59.219
-And your --
This is a long-time dentist?

00:01:59.219 --> 00:02:00.720
-Yeah.
I've been with him for years.

00:02:00.720 --> 00:02:01.754
He's my guy.
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:02.989
Well, let me tell you something.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:04.223
This is a great
advertisement for him,

00:02:04.223 --> 00:02:05.357
because your teeth
look fantastic.

00:02:05.357 --> 00:02:07.326
-Listen, I'm not telling anybody
what his name is

00:02:07.326 --> 00:02:09.228
because I'm afraid that
he'll become too busy for me.

00:02:09.228 --> 00:02:11.097
-Yeah, absolutely.

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:14.000
-And he, you know --
he's saved me

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.668
from some pretty sticky
situations.

00:02:15.668 --> 00:02:18.371
-Yeah, you had a dentist
actually save you --

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.472
a show-business save, right?

00:02:20.472 --> 00:02:21.674
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:25.078
Yeah, I broke my tooth
actually in half once.

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:26.912
-How do you break
a tooth in half?

00:02:26.912 --> 00:02:29.381
-So let me tell you, Seth.

00:02:29.381 --> 00:02:32.252
I have no beef
with Poland Springs.

00:02:32.252 --> 00:02:35.888
-No. The last thing you want
is a feud with Poland Springs.

00:02:35.888 --> 00:02:36.989
-Truly.
-Yeah.

00:02:36.989 --> 00:02:39.458
-But I did break
my tooth in half

00:02:39.458 --> 00:02:41.527
on a Poland Springs
water bottle.

00:02:41.527 --> 00:02:43.296
-Okay, now, can I jump in

00:02:43.296 --> 00:02:45.064
and say maybe
you were drinking it wrong?

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:48.067
[ Laughter ]

00:02:48.067 --> 00:02:52.238
-So basically, there's,
like, a little pull tab.

00:02:52.238 --> 00:02:56.042
You know the bottles that have,
like, the sucky thing?

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:59.145
-Yeah. Like the sort of,
like, sport top.

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:01.680
-Not the twist-off cap.
The sport top, yeah, yeah.

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:03.816
-Yeah.
-I was trying to open that.

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:05.385
-They originally called it
the sucky thing,

00:03:05.385 --> 00:03:07.920
and then marketing was like,
"Please. Anything."

00:03:07.920 --> 00:03:11.457
-"Anything but this."

00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:14.960
I was in the elevator bank
of my building at the time

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.730
and I was going to an audition
and I was opening my water

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:20.032
and I broke my tooth in half.
-Okay.

00:03:20.032 --> 00:03:22.067
-And I just remember
thinking, like --

00:03:22.067 --> 00:03:25.704
At no point was I like, "I can't
go to this audition now."

00:03:25.704 --> 00:03:27.506
I was kind of like,

00:03:27.506 --> 00:03:30.043
"Well, I guess I have to
go to this audition now

00:03:30.043 --> 00:03:33.045
with my tooth in my pocket."

00:03:33.045 --> 00:03:37.283
So, yeah.
So I put my tooth in my pocket.

00:03:37.283 --> 00:03:42.388
And I proceeded to go to
a Duane Reade on 34th Street.

00:03:42.388 --> 00:03:44.891
And I asked them
where their nail glue was.

00:03:44.891 --> 00:03:46.225
-Wow.

00:03:46.225 --> 00:03:47.760
-And they were like, "Aisle 9."

00:03:47.760 --> 00:03:50.129
And then I bought the nail glue

00:03:50.129 --> 00:03:51.897
and I said,
"Where's the bathroom?"

00:03:51.897 --> 00:03:53.333
And they said,
"We don't have one."

00:03:53.333 --> 00:03:56.235
And then they said the nearest
bathroom was in McDonald's.

00:03:56.235 --> 00:03:58.670
So I was like, "See you there."

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.139
I went to McDonald's.

00:04:00.139 --> 00:04:01.507
I asked them where
the bathroom was.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:02.908
They pointed me
in the direction.

00:04:02.908 --> 00:04:04.810
And when I got in there,
there was no mirror.

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:07.180
-Okay.
[ Laughs ]

00:04:07.180 --> 00:04:09.248
It would have been so awesome --
-'Cause 34th Street.

00:04:09.248 --> 00:04:10.716
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:10.716 --> 00:04:12.485
-If you had glued your tooth on
backwards, that would be --

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:14.387
[ Laughter ]

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:15.588
So did you have to do it --

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.356
just you had to, like,
feel your tooth?

00:04:17.356 --> 00:04:19.758
-Well, no, I had, like,
a small compact mirror...

00:04:19.758 --> 00:04:20.959
-Okay, gotcha.
Thank God.

00:04:20.959 --> 00:04:22.095
-...that I pulled out.

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:25.330
And I nail-glued my tooth
into my mouth

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:26.966
looking into this mirror.

00:04:26.966 --> 00:04:29.735
And then I went to the audition.

00:04:29.735 --> 00:04:31.370
And I got it.

00:04:31.370 --> 00:04:33.339
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:35.207 --> 00:04:36.576
-I can't help but noticing

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:38.911
your dentist didn't play a role
in that story at all.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.247
-[ Laughs ] Well, no.

00:04:41.247 --> 00:04:45.584
So -- So then --

00:04:45.584 --> 00:04:46.686
-You walked in his door

00:04:46.686 --> 00:04:48.921
and you're like,
"I don't need you anymore.

00:04:48.921 --> 00:04:51.790
I got some glue
from the Duane Reade.

00:04:51.790 --> 00:04:55.862
You're not getting my money."
-"What can you do for me?"

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:57.763
But then I did have to
go to the dentist

00:04:57.763 --> 00:04:59.264
'cause I needed him
to make it pretty.

00:04:59.264 --> 00:05:00.666
It was a little messy.

00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:02.835
-I can bet that if we actually
saw a photo from that day,

00:05:02.835 --> 00:05:04.904
we would be a little --
-I purposely took none.

00:05:04.904 --> 00:05:06.372
-That's very smart.

00:05:06.372 --> 00:05:09.842
-Because I was like, "I don't
want to remember this at all."

00:05:09.842 --> 00:05:12.244
But, yeah, then I then
went to see him,

00:05:12.244 --> 00:05:15.714
the man who is somewhere
adjacent to this building.

00:05:15.714 --> 00:05:21.453
And he was like, "What did you
use to put this together?

00:05:21.453 --> 00:05:23.689
I can't figure out
how to undo it."

00:05:23.689 --> 00:05:26.925
And I was like, "Nice."
-Yeah.

00:05:26.925 --> 00:05:29.529
That is an audition you landed.

00:05:29.529 --> 00:05:32.598
This is a fantastic story
with a very happy ending

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:34.633
that had a rough middle,
which is you auditioned

00:05:34.633 --> 00:05:36.101
for the first season
of "White Lotus."

00:05:36.101 --> 00:05:37.870
-I did.
-And got very close.

00:05:37.870 --> 00:05:39.872
-Yeah.
-And didn't get it.

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.440
-That's right.
-And...

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:42.675
[ Laughter ]

00:05:42.675 --> 00:05:45.244
Again, it has a happy ending.

00:05:45.244 --> 00:05:46.779
I would never do this
if it didn't.

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:49.782
But were you able then
to watch the first season

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:53.019
of "White Lotus," or was it,
like, sort of too raw a nerve?

00:05:53.019 --> 00:05:55.221
-No, oh, my God,
I was such a fan.

00:05:55.221 --> 00:05:56.822
I mean...

00:05:56.822 --> 00:05:58.357
Like, right off the bat.

00:05:58.357 --> 00:06:02.061
I feel like Mike is so good at
picking the exact right person

00:06:02.061 --> 00:06:03.762
that you watch the show
and you're like,

00:06:03.762 --> 00:06:05.764
"I just can't imagine
anybody else doing this."

00:06:05.764 --> 00:06:07.166
And that's exactly how I felt.

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:09.902
And I just feel, like, so lucky

00:06:09.902 --> 00:06:13.339
that for whatever reason,
I ended up getting to do it.

00:06:13.339 --> 00:06:14.473
Like, it's so cool.

00:06:14.473 --> 00:06:16.676
-It's so cool.
You're so wonderful in it.

00:06:16.676 --> 00:06:19.044
I think the same is true of you,

00:06:19.044 --> 00:06:21.647
which is I don't think anybody
who would've wanted that part

00:06:21.647 --> 00:06:23.716
could watch you and think that
it could be done any better.

00:06:23.716 --> 00:06:25.051
And you got to spend time
in Sicily.

00:06:25.051 --> 00:06:26.318
That must have been
a fantastic place to shoot.

00:06:26.318 --> 00:06:27.953
-So much time in Sicily, yeah.

00:06:27.953 --> 00:06:29.789
It was amazing.
It was incredible.

00:06:29.789 --> 00:06:31.690
-And my friend Aubrey Plaza,

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:32.992
who's wonderful on the show,
as well --

00:06:32.992 --> 00:06:35.127
-She's great.
-And someone -- This --

00:06:35.127 --> 00:06:37.130
So you guys
went hiking together.

00:06:37.130 --> 00:06:38.697
-We did.
-Who was in charge of the hike?

00:06:38.697 --> 00:06:41.100
-So it was me, technically.
-Okay.

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:45.471
-It was a place that I had
hiked to several times before,

00:06:45.471 --> 00:06:47.039
and then I did get us lost.

00:06:47.039 --> 00:06:50.076
-Okay. So you confidently
told her, "I know this hike.

00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:51.210
Don't worry."
-100%.

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:54.046
I was like,
"Follow me right over here."

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:56.982
And then we got so lost
that we ended up

00:06:56.982 --> 00:07:00.086
sort of walking down
the side of the highway.

00:07:00.086 --> 00:07:01.487
-Okay, that's never a good sign
on a hike.

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:03.155
-No, no, no, no.

00:07:03.155 --> 00:07:05.324
Yeah, so -- And there was no --

00:07:05.324 --> 00:07:06.492
I mean, there's no sidewalk.

00:07:06.492 --> 00:07:08.227
It's just you're just sort of
on the road.

00:07:08.227 --> 00:07:10.128
And it was kind of funny
because there was

00:07:10.128 --> 00:07:14.633
this whole sort of biker gang
that came, like, past us.

00:07:14.633 --> 00:07:17.469
And it was a very
Daphne/Harper moment

00:07:17.469 --> 00:07:19.104
because Aubrey was like --

00:07:19.104 --> 00:07:20.906
They were like, "Hey, girls."

00:07:20.906 --> 00:07:22.274
And she was like,
"Don't look at me."

00:07:22.274 --> 00:07:24.643
And I was like, "Hi!"

00:07:24.643 --> 00:07:27.246
-It is a little unfair to say,
"Don't look at me,"

00:07:27.246 --> 00:07:29.715
when you're walking
on the side of the highway.

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:32.451
I think at some point
you want people to look at you,

00:07:32.451 --> 00:07:34.720
you know, just out of safety.
-Yeah. She had a bucket hat on.

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.221
She was, like,
trying to be really low-key.

00:07:36.221 --> 00:07:39.825
And I was like,
"I love it here!"

00:07:39.825 --> 00:07:40.993
-Thank you so much
for being here.

00:07:40.993 --> 00:07:42.461
I can't wait
for the final episode.

00:07:42.461 --> 00:07:44.630
Thank you for not spoiling it.
-Thank you for having me.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:46.532
-You guys, that's Meghann Fahy.

00:07:46.532 --> 00:07:48.233
Season finale
of "The White Lotus"

00:07:48.233 --> 00:07:50.970
airs this Sunday at 9:00 p.m.
on HBO and HBO Max.

00:07:50.970 --> 00:07:52.405
We'll be right back
with more "Late Night."

